WEBVTT

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:37.030
Heroes One More Time

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:45.960
What did you say, Jose?!

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:49.680
Are your ears going now too as well, Nero?

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:52.100
If I hadn't covered you that time...

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:55.140
this town of Gloria would have been destroyed.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:57.310
When I deliver a hit, it's perfect.

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:01.020
No matter what type of Armor, I've never failed to bring it down.

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:04.070
It was because of my support.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:07.530
I've had enough. I'm through cleaning up your mess.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.610
You call yourself the leader...

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:10.570
What's that?!

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:13.240
Oh, you want to fight?

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:14.870
If you do.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:17.750
Excuse me, both of you, please stop it.

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:19.460
Don't stop me, Yukiko.

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:21.330
Yeah. There's no need to worry.

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:24.630
No one's worrying about you guys.

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:25.420
Franco.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:27.840
The ruckus you create is bad for business.

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:31.470
You're not the only customers here.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:34.730
We've been coming here since before you were born, sonny!

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:37.640
Then why don't you quiet down and act your age.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:41.600
Act our age? How dare you speak to us like that?

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:43.440
You've got no right to be calling us old-timers...

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:44.610
You're old, aren't you?

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:45.320
What?!

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:48.070
Sit down. Both of you.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:50.700
All right.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:52.910
Sorry, Yukiko.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.660
No, that's all right, Barrio.

00:02:57.950 --> 00:02:59.330
Shouldn't have done that.

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:07.630
What should we do? You want me to spell it out for them?

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:08.590
What?

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:10.670
Tell them not to come back here again.

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:13.760
But they're Grandma's friends.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:16.050
You can't always be thinking about your grandmother...

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:17.060
Excuse me! You can't always be thinking about your grandmother...

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:21.140
I'd like some milk and some lunch, please!

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:22.350
Yes.

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:24.980
And a bucket of water.

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:32.570
Are you awake?!

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.320
It's a real nuisance when you get so hungry that you collapse!

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:38.160
Do you realize how hard it was to carry you here?

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:41.120
Excuse me, waitress...

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:42.210
Yes?

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:47.130
I'd like your cheapest meal and all the condiments you've got.

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:51.340
So, where did you come from?

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:52.590
Evergreen.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.590
Oh, him too?

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:55.720
No.

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:57.180
He's not with you?

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:59.100
- Well, we're together now but...

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:00.350
- It's sweet!
- Well, we're together now but...

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:02.020
That's for sure.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.850
That's great. It sounds like a lot of fun.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.980
You're traveling, right?

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:11.900
Yeah, I guess you could say that...

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:16.110
Hello there.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:17.320
Hello.

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:18.660
I'm Nero.

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:19.830
I'm Jose.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.410
I'm Barrio, and that's Carlos.

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:25.210
Your name?

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:26.170
Van.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:28.250
People call me, "Van, the Man of Steel."

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:33.970
You're the one who took down the Bridge City Baron?

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:36.470
And defeated the Wild Bunch as well?

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:38.220
Yeah... I'm afraid so.

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:40.350
We like you!

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:42.930
Eat. Tacos are good for you.

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:45.940
Oh, but I don't have money...

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:47.190
Leave it to us!

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:00.410
Hey, Bucci.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:02.660
What do you want?

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:04.870
Nothing all that important.

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:07.540
The mayor wanted to know whether or not...

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:11.170
you'll be at the meeting at the Town Hall tomorrow.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:12.050
Oh...

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:14.420
Sorry, but I'm busy.

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:17.090
Oh, is that right?

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:18.550
I know it.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:22.220
You don't want me to come, do you?

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:25.890
No! That's not it!

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:29.100
But I guess there's nothing I can do if you're busy.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:33.070
Bucci... don't tell me...

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:35.820
you're doing another one of your experiments!

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:41.620
I'm sure you understand this too.

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:44.950
We Armor riders live life right on the edge!

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:45.750
Yeah.

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:47.710
No, you don't understand!

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:51.630
The Armor back in our day was a real pain in the ass!

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:53.040
Enough already!

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.420
You're ruining our drink.

00:05:55.510 --> 00:05:57.800
Take your tall tales to the old folks home!

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:00.720
You fought using an Armor in this one horse town?

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:03.470
All that alcohol must be affecting your memories!

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:06.060
Every night it's the same story!

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:08.480
Let's see it. Show us your Armor!

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:12.900
Armor's not something for showing off!

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:19.950
Learn how to handle your own body before you try and operate an Armor.

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:26.490
Old man, you'd better show us the Armor if you don't want your ass kicked.

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:29.750
Idiot! We'd never pull out the Armor on someone who's empty handed!

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.000
Oh, is that right?!

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:32.790
- Let'em have it!
- Do it! Beat them up!

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:34.500
Hey, people!

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:37.050
Leave them alone. It's good medicine.

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:37.880
Franco!

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:40.090
Van, stop them!

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:41.970
I'm against violence.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:43.010
Come on!

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:48.520
What's the matter? You don't have to hold back.

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:52.020
Bring it on, you babe in the woods.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:53.940
Say, this is getting ugly, don't you think?

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:57.440
Old man, let's call this thing off. We're sorry.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:00.490
We went too far as well. And losing control isn't good for you.

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:02.570
Don't make fun of us!

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:07.910
Do you remember?

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:13.960
Beneath the sky's swirling nighttime fog

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:25.760
You told me your great dream

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:38.520
Anyone, everyone In exchange for growing up

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:39.320
She's like Chizuru when she sings.

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:43.240
We leave behind the things we treasure
She's like Chizuru when she sings.

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:50.750
We leave behind the things we treasure

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:54.730
But don't forget the rainbow

00:07:54.760 --> 00:08:00.380
The one we saw that time that day...

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:13.730
Well, I'd better get going.

00:08:13.730 --> 00:08:14.520
What?

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:15.730
Where are you going?

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:17.520
I'll camp out somewhere nearby.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:19.270
I know a place!

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:21.980
There's a good spot.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:24.780
That's all right. Thanks for the food.

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:25.950
Don't be so uptight!

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:27.660
You're one of us.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:28.910
Please don't follow me.

00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:31.540
We'll teach you a few things about riding an Armor.

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:32.790
Like I said, stay away.

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:36.370
Back when I was fighting the Saurus Empire...

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.000
Don't come!

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.290
Sing the victory song!

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:43.460
Oh, I'm sorry. Go ahead and make yourself at home.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:44.470
Yes.

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:46.630
You like books?

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:49.640
Mine were all burned.

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:52.680
Go ahead and take one if you'd like.

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:56.140
Oh no, that's too much. I feel bad just for staying here.

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:57.440
That's all right.

00:08:57.690 --> 00:09:00.270
Maybe you could tell me about your travels in return?

00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:01.520
For my reference.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:02.230
Sure!

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:06.780
Let's see, my town is covered with rocks...

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:11.450
Say, Yukiko, won't you leave this town together with me?

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:14.700
I can't do that. I have the restaurant.

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:17.870
You want to spend your whole life in this god-forsaken place?

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:21.340
Keeping company with the old-timers everyday.

00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:27.800
But Grandma ran this place all by herself in order to raise me.

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:29.390
Well...

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:31.850
Have you heard enough?

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:33.600
Yeah. Thanks.

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:35.140
Great.

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:38.230
Oh, your song earlier was wonderful.

00:09:39.190 --> 00:09:41.860
My grandma taught it to me.

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:45.150
The old-timers love it.

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:47.280
Oh, that's why.

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:52.700
Chizuru also said that you mustn't show off your Armor.

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:55.580
However, if it's out of necessity...

00:09:55.750 --> 00:09:58.000
It's the heroic spirit that moves it!

00:09:58.290 --> 00:09:59.250
I understand.

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:00.920
You don't understand!

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:03.840
You need another 10 years before you'll be a true Armor rider.

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:07.840
10 years from now I won't be alive.

00:10:09.010 --> 00:10:09.840
To Chizuru!

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:10.970
Brindis!

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:13.350
Our Pink Amigo!

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:16.020
Say, do you know Chizuru?

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:17.100
No, I don't.

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:18.640
How come?!

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:21.020
She could out-drink anyone.

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:23.230
She could out-brawl anyone.

00:10:23.230 --> 00:10:28.690
She still watches over us, along with the Pink Amigo.

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:30.740
You drink too!

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:33.120
No, I don't drink.

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:35.330
Tequila's good for you.

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:36.120
Like I said!

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:51.720
Good morning everyone.

00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:54.260
The regular town meeting will take place as scheduled...

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:54.890
Van!
The regular town meeting will take place as scheduled...

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:57.390
Where did you go yesterday?

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:03.350
Hey, could you help me gather information later?

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:05.940
Sure... But what about the old-timers?

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:07.440
Let us out!

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:09.780
Why did you put us in this place?

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:11.490
That's enough!

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:13.240
Hey chief, let us out!

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:16.280
The reason we get complaints is because you raise such a racket.

00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:20.910
Young people all over town are laughing at you.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:24.170
Do they know about what we did for them?

00:11:24.170 --> 00:11:25.290
That's for sure!

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:27.840
The people who don't know now outnumber those who do.

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:30.880
I'm asking you, please be quiet.

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:33.720
How long are you going to cling to the past?

00:11:33.930 --> 00:11:37.930
I don't want to do these things to my childhood heroes.

00:11:39.140 --> 00:11:40.270
Little Mabo...

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:44.440
The police can handle things in this town now.

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:47.320
The days of the hero are over.

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:51.610
Everyone, I'm the Mayor, Walter.

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:56.620
I am truly thankful to you all for attending this regular town meeting.

00:11:57.070 --> 00:12:01.500
Now, the crime rate in our town of Gloria has dropped below 1 percent.

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:05.330
This proves that the citizens of this town...

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:07.920
have all become dear neighbors and found mutual understanding.

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:09.000
And so I am truly...

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:10.800
What's that?

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:15.840
Hey, that sound is!

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:18.850
No, it can't be!

00:12:18.850 --> 00:12:19.560
It's...

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:20.560
There's no mistake.

00:12:24.190 --> 00:12:24.980
Armor?

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:27.310
That's right! Look!

00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:31.110
This is my Armor! Respect it!

00:12:31.110 --> 00:12:32.650
I made it!

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:36.240
This place isn't safe either. We need to get out of here!

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:37.780
Sorry...

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:39.280
There's something we need to do.

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:40.080
What?

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:42.200
If we don't come back...

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:45.830
tell Yukiko and the other youngsters...

00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:48.290
that we're sorry.

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:50.210
You can't be serious...

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:53.590
You people!

00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:58.930
Turning me into an outcast just because I made one mistake!

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:00.890
Hurry up and arrest Bucci!

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:03.310
But he's got an Armor!

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:07.900
Yukiko! Let's escape to the hilltop with the others!

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:08.810
Yes.

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:10.560
You hurry up too!

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:11.360
Yes!

00:13:12.070 --> 00:13:12.860
Van!

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:15.070
Hey, you can use your Armor to!

00:13:15.070 --> 00:13:17.570
No. I've got no reason to help.

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:19.160
Reason?

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:21.490
Idiot!

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:26.000
Understand that I am doing this for the town's sake!

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:30.250
It's using a system similar to Dann...

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:32.630
What?

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:40.890
This is our town.

00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:44.890
Yukiko!

00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:49.600
I could have used this strength to bring everyone happiness!

00:13:54.610 --> 00:13:55.740
Grandma's...

00:13:57.110 --> 00:13:58.280
Don't!

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:00.110
Grandma's!

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:02.950
Grandma's! The restaurant!

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:05.700
Someone! Someone save Grandma's!

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:09.540
Leave it to us.

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:18.420
What the hell is that?

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:24.310
Could it be?

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:26.810
Take a good look, youngster.

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:29.810
That right there! That spirit!

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:33.480
That's what a legendary hero is!

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:37.150
Barrio, I want you covering Carlos!

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:38.320
Got it.

00:14:38.990 --> 00:14:42.160
All right! Scramble Advancer!

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:50.920
You stupid old heroes!

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:53.130
The El Gran attack isn't working!

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:56.420
Nero, don't make me clean up after you!

00:14:56.420 --> 00:14:57.130
Jose?

00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:59.840
You know what this calls for?

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:01.930
Sounds good to me.

00:15:02.180 --> 00:15:04.970
Let's go! El Dorado!

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:38.800
Five Unit Combination! El Dora Four!

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:40.920
What the?

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:42.880
So it's true?

00:15:43.470 --> 00:15:45.050
It's the first time I've ever seen it.

00:15:45.140 --> 00:15:45.890
Old-timers!

00:15:45.890 --> 00:15:48.220
Free-fall Grazie!

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:52.390
I won't allow it!

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:55.100
To hell with your useless combined system!

00:15:58.940 --> 00:15:59.650
Our arm!

00:15:59.820 --> 00:16:02.360
Perfect! If I bring you down...

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:05.570
the townspeople will accept me!

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:11.000
Nero! Fire while we try and hold him off!

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:11.540
Right!

00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:17.500
Damn it.

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:20.300
I shouldn't have had so much to drink.

00:16:20.630 --> 00:16:21.420
Nero.

00:16:22.550 --> 00:16:24.090
Don't miss this time.

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:26.760
Have faith in your leader.

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:30.470
Bombardier!

00:16:32.310 --> 00:16:33.390
Why are you doing this?

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:38.060
Didn't they make fun of you too?! Didn't they say they didn't need you?!

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:40.020
Am I wrong?!

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:44.150
No one understands or accepts you!

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:48.870
So then why?! Why do you still protect this town?!

00:16:49.280 --> 00:16:50.280
Why?!

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:53.370
Sonny boy is still wet behind the ears.

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:56.370
We don't want those kinds of things.

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:57.710
Right.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:00.420
As long as we can protect the people's memories...

00:17:00.420 --> 00:17:01.380
that's all...

00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:02.920
That's all...

00:17:03.130 --> 00:17:04.220
That's all...

00:17:04.630 --> 00:17:06.590
That's all we want.

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:08.800
It can't be!

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:10.350
Even you guys are...

00:17:10.350 --> 00:17:12.260
making fun of me!

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:13.100
Old-timers!

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:18.100
I guess it wasn't complete after all.

00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:22.730
Just as the name suggests, it needs the fifth unit to make Eldora Five.

00:17:23.190 --> 00:17:27.660
But now they're one body short on power and energy.

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:29.030
One body?

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:35.330
Yes, Yukiko's grandmother. Chizuru's Pink Amigo.

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:46.170
Do you remember?

00:17:46.550 --> 00:17:51.300
Beneath the sky's swirling nighttime fog

00:17:52.050 --> 00:18:01.480
You told me your great dream

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:05.320
Anyone, everyone in exchange for growing up

00:18:05.320 --> 00:18:06.570
We can't lose.
Anyone, everyone in exchange for growing up

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:06.690
Anyone, everyone in exchange for growing up

